WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:09.400
From which location was flight MH17 shot down, and how was the weapon brought there and removed again?

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:13.400
The investigation team was able to answer those questions.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.900
In this respect a large quantity of evidence has been gathered.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:24.900
We have analysed the location of the telephone towers which received signals from the telephones of the officers escorting the Buk convoy.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.900
Telephone traffic between those officers and their commanders was recorded on several occasions.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:36.900
During those intercepted conversations they speak about where they are and the route to be followed.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:41.400
There are numerous witnesses who saw the Buk TELAR pass by.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:47.400
Especially after last year's call to the public, many persons reported that they were willing to testify.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:53.900
The Buk TELAR was photographed and filmed several times while being transported along that route.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.400
The photographs and video clips that the team found on social media were checked for authenticity.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:12.900
All telecom data and intercepted telephone calls that have been examined by the investigation team demonstrate that the Buk TELAR was brought into Ukraine from the Russian Federation.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:20.900
Subsequently the weapon was transported in a convoy with separatists from eastern Ukraine to the final launch site.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.900
How did they proceed?

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:28.900
Around 8:00 in the morning a witness saw the convoy with the Buk TELAR in Yenakiieve.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:41.900
In the previous hours the convoy had travelled along a certain route from the Russian border, as appears from telecom information, including the following intercepted telephone conversation.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:27.900
“The Buk TELAR crossed the line”, in other words passed the border, and was transported on a trailer: a white Volvo truck with a red low-loader.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:38.900
On several photographs and videos that we found on social media and otherwise, the Volvo can be seen bearing the Buk TELAR with anti-aircraft missiles under a camouflage net.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:44.900
Witnesses that we have spoken to also testified that they had seen this vehicle with four missiles.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:49.900
The truck was escorted by a Volkswagen Transporter and a UAZ jeep.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:54.900
The escorting officers were several armed men wearing uniforms.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:05.900
In Donetsk the convoy stopped for some time at two locations: first at a crossing, and later on, after the convoy had turned around, it stood still on a strip at the side of the Makiivka highway.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:13.900
In Donetsk the convoy was seen by many witnesses, and frequent reports about this convoy appeared in social media.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:18.900
Paris Match published a photograph of the convoy in Donetsk in its magazine.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:22.400
This photograph was a so-called still from a video.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:31.400
In the meantime the investigation team has obtained the original video footage of the transport in Donetsk.

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:44.900
Starting at 11:00 hours the convoy continued on main road 21 in the direction of Makiivka, Zuhres, Torez and ultimately Snizhne.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:49.900
Several moving images have been made that show the truck with the Buk TELAR.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:57.900
These videos, which are in the hands of the investigation team, were made in Makiivka and in Zuhres.

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:16.900
In Torez the convoy was also seen multiple times, of which the investigation team has managed to obtain new images clearly showing the Buk TELAR and the escorting vehicles.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:25.400
For safety reasons relating to the person who actually made these images, the background has been cut out.

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:31.400
Around midday the white Volvo low-loader with the Buk TELAR arrived in Snizhne.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:36.900
In Snizhne the Buk TELAR was loaded off the truck near the Furshet supermarket.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:40.900
From there on the Buk TELAR drove further on its own.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:44.400
In Snizhne it passed by an apartment building.

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:54.900
Then the last moving images of the Buk TELAR that are available show the system while driving towards its final destination.

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:16.900
This final destination is farmland near Pervomaiskyi.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:24.900
This is 21 km south-east of the spot where flight MH17 crashed, around twenty past four in the afternoon.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:32.900
The investigation team has collected a large amount of evidence for the determination of the precise launch site of the Buk missile.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:41.900
This evidence shows without any doubt that this farmland near Pervomaiskyi can be pointed out as the launch site.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:45.900
What does the evidence consist of?

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:50.900
The investigation team has recorded statements of many witnesses.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:55.400
Some witnesses were very close to the launch site when the missile was launched.

00:05:55.500 --> 00:06:02.400
These witnesses spoke about a very loud noise, a violent explosion and a high whistling sound.

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:13.900
Other witnesses have testified that they had seen a plume of smoke, that they had seen the Buk TELAR at the launch site in Pervomaiskyi, and immediately afterwards saw the missile that had been launched.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:18.900
In addition, some witnesses testified that they had seen an airplane crashing.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:22.900
Several witnesses had seen the inversion trail of the missile.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:27.900
The witnesses described the trail as white, very thick and very long.

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:34.900
This photograph of the inversion trail was made in Torez and was distributed through social media.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:38.900
The photo was examined by the Netherlands Forensic Institute.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:43.900
The NFI does not have any indications that this photo was manipulated.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:52.900
The Dutch meteorological institute also examined the photo, and they note that this was not a cloud or an airplane's contrail.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:07:01.900
In addition, in the spring of 2016, after long research on social media, the investigation team found two new photos.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:08.900
Since it is difficult to see the inversion trail on the photographs, we show you the photos with a filter.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:19.900
An analysis of visibility lines was made of the first photo and the statements of witnesses: the direction in which the witness was looking when he or she saw or photographed the trail.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:28.900
The spot where these visibility lines come together is located very close to the aforementioned farmland near Pervomaiskyi.

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:37.900
There are also intercepted telephone conversations which refer to the launch location, among which the following conversation.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:09.400
The telephone of one of the participants to this conversation connects with the telephone tower which is located closest to the launch site.

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:19.400
In addition, the description of the surroundings in this conversation, the field and the forest, corresponds with the surroundings of the launch site in Pervomaiskyi.

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:23.400
Several journalists went to the launch site near Pervomaiskyi.

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:26.900
Some of them were shown a piece of land which had been burned.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:31.900
They saw some scorched land measuring about 30 by 30 metres.

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:44.900
Other journalists spoke to inhabitants of the area, who told them that the field had been on fire on the 17th of July 2014, and that they had ploughed the field in order to prevent the whole field from catching fire.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:49.400
It was clearly visible that the field had been ploughed.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:58.900
The investigation team, who as you may recall did not have access to this area after the crash, has also interviewed witnesses about this location.

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:06.900
The satellite images which were made of this location on the 16th of July and the 21st of July were also examined.

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:11.900
Because of the cloudy weather, images from the days in between could not be used.

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:16.900
The images before and after the crash show significant differences.

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:25.900
The photo of the 21st of July shows the charred and ploughed piece of land that could not yet be seen on the photo of the 16th of July.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:31.900
The 21st of July photo also shows tracks of caterpillar vehicles.

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:35.900
Immediately after the launch the Buk TELAR was removed.

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:43.900
There are hardly any images of the route along which the system was removed, since this took place late in the evening and during the night.

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:55.900
However, we have been able to partially establish the route through analysis of telecommunication data and on the basis of the statement of a separatist who was involved in the removal of the Buk TELAR.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:10:01.400
It is believed that the Buk TELAR drove in the direction of Snizhne autonomously.

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:08.400
There it was reloaded onto the white Volvo low-loader in the late evening hours of the 17th of July.

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:14.900
From there the low-loader went to Krasnyi Luch and then via Debaltseve to Luhansk.

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:21.900
In Luhansk in the early morning a video was made of the Volvo truck with the low-loader carrying the Buk TELAR.

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:27.400
One can see that at this point in time there are only three missiles on the installation.

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:33.900
From there the transport moved on to the Russian border and then crossed that border.

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:40.900
The JIT has intercepted telephone conversations which took place in the morning of the 18th of July 2014.

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:49.900
These conversations demonstrate that at that moment the Buk TELAR was already back in the Russian Federation.
